{"type":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"call-b5a9f598-2eca-4136-8349-cbd48b92f4fd-26","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"1→{\n  \"text\": \"I'll start by reading the Batch E file list and the existing Batch A–D notes so the new fighter annotations match the same format.Next I’ll match Batch A–D annotation style and pull the source `.as` files for this batch.I’ll scan fighter.xml and the existing annotation generator so Batch E notes stay consistent with earlier batches.I’ll extract metadata from every Batch E `.as` first, then generate the notes from that so the large timelines stay complete.I have the Batch E patterns. Next I’ll generate the annotations with a parser that matches the Batch A–D note format.All 67 notes are generated. I’ll spot-check MainTimeline, 全动作, and a few stubs against the source next.Several systematic issues showed up (engine relative paths, duplicate constructors, missed `$` fields). I’ll fix the generator and regenerate.Notes check out. I’ll write the Batch E index and mark E done in the fighters overview.Batch E 已闭合：清单里 67 个 `.as` 都有对应注记，F–G 未动。\\n\\n索引：\\n- [`reverse/line-by-line/fighters/00-BATCH-E-INDEX.md`](reverse/line-by-line/fighters/00-BATCH-E-INDEX.md)（67/67）\\n- [`reverse/line-by-line/fighters/00-INDEX.md`](reverse/line-by-line/fighters/00-INDEX.md) 已标 **E done**，F–G 仍 pending\\n\\n| 块 | XML | 形态 | 脚本帧（动作 MC） |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 鸣人 | `naruto` / `naruto_yw` / `naruto_sw` | F2→F3→F4，`doWanKai` | 95 / 93 / 93 |\\n| 仙人·黄金 | `naruto_xianren` / `naruto_gold` | F2→F3 | 109 / 115 |\\n| 宁次 | `neji` | 单形态 | 101（类名 `一护全动作_1`） |\\n| 带土 | `obito` / `obito_s2` | F2→F3 | 87（`樱_1`）/ 101（`鸣人全动作_14`） |\\n| 织姬 | `orihime` | 单形态 | 119 |\\n\\n本批共性：全是拳防。AI 面一律缺 `kbsmian`（仙人/黄金有空必 HitVO，盒仍缺）。仙人黄金、带土无 `snd_*`。织姬多帧 `addHp(recoveryBisha=3)`。带土真面目 HitVO 数值夸张（`tk3` 600、`kj14` 850、`hurtTime` 30000+）。未改 `decompiled/`，未开 F–G。\",\n  \"stopReason\": \"end_turn\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"01a06eb3-0f81-7fb3-8f3c-af00a90b37f7\",\n  \"requestId\": \"7de47e7b-d342-4c21-9b98-7321eaf677c7\",\n  \"thought\": \"The user wants me to continue a reverse engineering task for Batch E of fighters. Let me start by reading the relevant skills and understanding the task structure.\\nThis is a documentation/annotation task of ActionScript fighter files, not binary reverse engineering. I should look at the quality reference from previous batches and the existing INDEX files. Let me...I have a good understanding of the format. Now I need to look at a large action MC annotation for reference, and also look at all the source files. Let me also look at a 全动作 annotation to understand h...This is a large documentation task. I'll write a Python script to generate annotations from the AS files, matching the quality of previous batches. Let me first look at how previous batches may have b...There's a grok-fighters-E.log that might have previous attempts. Let me also look at fighter.xml details for these characters, and look at previous generation scripts if any exist. Also check if there...There's already a grok-fighters-E.log - maybe a previous attempt started. Let me also look at existing generator scripts. Given the volume of files (67 AS files totaling ~10k lines), I should write a ...Let me look at HitType.md fully and also look at a complete 全动作 file from Batch D to understand the grouping algorithm. Then I'll write a comprehensive Python generator.\\nI have a clear picture. I'll write a comprehensive Python generator that produces documentation matching the Batch A-D format. Let me look at more method annotations used in previous batches so I can ...I have a very clear picture of the expected output format. I'll write a comprehensive Python generator that:\\nGot it — Batch E is locked in. I'll generate the annotated MDs for all 67 fighters (naruto, naruto_xr, neji, obito, orihime) using the exact style from A–D, plus the index files.\\n\\nStarting with the parser now. 67 files should be manageable if I keep the output consistent. Let me pull the first few and start writing.Interesting notes:\\n- neji MainTimeline has no defineHurtSound even though there are snd_* files. Need to verify.Got it — continuing the 长城任务 with fighters Batch E only.\\n\\nI’ll start by scanning the file list and building the annotated MDs for each `.as` under `/workspace/bvn-3.3/reverse/line-by-line/fighters/`, following the exact structure from A–D.\\n\\nFirst, let me 00-BATCH-E-INDEX.md and the per-fighter files.\\n\\n**00-BATCH-E-INDEX.md** (draft)\\n\\n```markdown\\n# Batch E — 2025-06-?? fighters\\n\\nFighters: naruto, naruto_xr, neji, obito, orihime  \\nTotal 67 .My regex for sounds failed because neji uses multiple arguments: `defineHurtSound(snd_hurt1,snd_hurt2,snd_hurt3)`. I need to handle that.\\nThe regex failed because defineAction objects span multiple lines and my `[^}]+` might have issues... wait, I used `\\\\{([^}]+)\\\\}` which should work. Let me debug... Oh the issue is `this.defineAction` ...Got it — Batch E fighters are up next. I'll start by pulling the file list and mapping out the structure for naruto, naruto_xr, neji, obito, and orihime.I have a solid understanding. Time to write a comprehensive generator. I'll make it high quality to match previous batches.\\nGot it — Batch E is locked in. I'll generate the annotated Markdown files for the five fighters (naruto, naruto_xr, neji, obito, orihime) under `/workspace/bvn-3.3/reverse/line-by-line/fighters/`, plus the batch index and update the main 00-INDEX.md. All Chinese, matching the style from A–D.\\n\\nStarting with naruto now. 67 files total, so I'll do one fighter at a time and echo progress after each. Ready when you are.I have enough to write a high-quality generator. Let me also look at how previous batches documented fire() with object literals.\\nGot it — I'll use the compact `fire()` form and the updated `defineHurtSound` regex for multi-arg calls. The ID meaning function looks solid too.\\n\\nNow 