{"type":"thought","data":"Got it — the two bugs are clear now."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\n1."}
{"type":"thought","data":" `parse_kv_object` is choking on quoted keys like `\"power\":20` because it’s treating the colon as a plain separator instead of respecting the quotes."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\n2."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The `extra_calls` splitter is mis-handling the `if(!this."}
{"type":"thought","data":"$fighter_ctr ller){ return; }` block because it lacks a trailing semicolon after the closing brace."}
{"type":"thought","data":" When we skip `defineAction` calls, the buffered `if` statement never gets flushed (no `;` after `}`), so the next top-level statement (`defineBishaFace`) gets concatenated to it, producing the 296-line merge."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nI’ll fix both in the next pass:\n\n- Update `parse_kv_object` to handle quoted keys properly."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n- Improve the statement splitter: after `}` that drops depth to 0, treat it as a complete statement even without `;`, and flush `if` blocks immediately."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n- Also fix the `if` special-case in extra_calls so it doesn’t skip the merged line."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nOnce those are in, I’ll regenerate the Batch F annotations (orochimaru, pain, renji, rukia, sakura, sasuke, sasuke_xz) and update the index files."}
